  "title": "Globalization, Containerization and the Oil System",
  "summary": "The reacceleration of globalization depended on transport standards, energy and institutions working together. Containerization reduced transfer costs across transport modes, while oil supplied dense energy for mobility, industry and logistics, allowing long-distance production networks to expand.",
